# Repository-root Docker context for the future backend image.
# Keep solution/test sources so solution-level restore/build remains possible.
# Git retention and Docker build inputs have separate purposes.
.git
**/.git
.gitignore
.agents
.codex
.aws
AGENTS.md
README.md
SNAPSHOT.md
docs
frontend-docs
review
evidence
**/evidence
artifacts
test-results
compose*.yaml
compose*.yml
docker-compose*.yaml
docker-compose*.yml
**/*.http
**/TestResults
**/test-results
**/output
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/packages
**/.nuget
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.playwright
**/playwright-report
**/.cache
**/logs
**/log
**/*.log
**/*.trx
**/*.binlog
**/*.pid
**/*.tmp
**/*.swp
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/*.code-workspace
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Credentials and local configuration never belong in the build context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.envrc
**/*.env
**/appsettings.[Ll]ocal.json
**/appsettings.*.[Ll]ocal.json
**/http-client.private.env.json
**/secrets.json
**/.secrets
**/*.private.*
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.snk

# global.json, *.sln, *.csproj, dotnet-tools.json, source, migrations,
# shared/environment appsettings, and future Dockerfile/railway config stay included.
